You are triaging BUG-50 (a Bug). Report: removing the last IP from the allowlist shows a blank screen instead of the empty state. Repro steps from the report: add a single IP, remove it, the panel goes blank. The responsible component in the repo:

```tsx
// src/components/AllowlistPanel.tsx
export function AllowlistPanel({ ips, onRemove }: Props) {
  if (ips.length === 0) {
    return; // returns undefined
  }
  return (
    <ul>
      {ips.map((ip) => (
        <li key={ip}>{ip} <button onClick={() => onRemove(ip)}>Remove</button></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
// src/components/EmptyState.tsx exists (renders the 'no IPs yet' prompt) but is not referenced here.
```

Reproduce, find the cause, and scope the fix.

Triage BUG-52 (a Bug): a NullPointerException is thrown when rendering the user row for some users. Repro from the report: open the admin user list containing a user created via the invite flow — that row's render crashes. The relevant code:

```kotlin
// UserRowRenderer.kt
fun render(user: UserEntity): Row {
  val display = user.profile!!.displayName // NPE thrown here
  // ...
}

// InviteService.kt — createInvitedUser() inserts the user record but never creates a profile
